  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 141 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday...Upper ridging will strengthen across the \nCentral U.S. as troughing will persist across the western U.S. with \na closed low of the coast of central California on Wednesday moving \ninland Thursday. Highs warm into the 70s Wednesday and Thursday. \n\nThursday night through Friday...The lead shortwave trough \nwithin the main western U.S. upper trough is forecast to fill \nand lift into the Northern Plains. This will drive a cold front \ninto the area Friday night. Will see an increase in moisture \nahead of the front, with dewpoints in the 50s Thursday and \nFriday. Southerly winds will also increase to 15 to 25 mph \nacross the west on Thursday, and windy Friday area wide, at 20 \nto 30 mph with gusts to 40 mph. \n\nCould see a few showers in advance of the system Thursday night\ninto Friday, with increased chances for showers and a few \nthunderstorms Friday night into Saturday as the main upper \ntrough lifts through the region and interacts with the front. \nHighs warm into the upper 70s Thursday and Friday, cooling into \nthe upper 50s to upper 60s Saturday and mid 60s Sunday.",
